  "id": "COMPOUND:526 - DISEASE:799",
  "verbalization": "Nortriptyline appears to influence Dentinogenesis Imperfecta through a shared pathway involving the sushi domain containing 3 protein. This protein, which is affected by nortriptyline, leads to the development of Dental Plaque, a condition that is causally linked to multiple downstream targets. These include Wnt family member 7A and gamma-glutamyltransferase light chain 2, both of which contribute to the pathogenesis of Dentinogenesis Imperfecta. The evidence suggests that nortriptyline may modulate the expression or function of these proteins, thereby impacting the development of the condition. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which nortriptyline could exert its effects, though the exact nature of the molecular interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple overlapping pathways underscores the complexity of the disease and the potential for nortriptyline to act as a therapeutic agent through a broader biological network.",
